      en: "The Sombor County Hall (Županija Sombor) was built in 1882 in the Neo-Renaissance style. It originally housed the county administration and later served as the city hall. The facade features elaborate sculptures and a prominent tower. Inside, ornate halls are decorated with frescoes and stucco ceilings. The building reflects the political history of Vojvodina and its autonomy within the Habsburg Monarchy. It currently houses municipal offices and cultural institutions.",
